{"c":[{"id":"55288e90aa520159","sum":"v1: .scratch/ never committed; Screenpipe sidecar (own screenpipe@0.4.50 :3031) behind hard-failing last-N; /search needs Bearer SCREENPIPE_LOCAL_API_KEY + X-Screenpipe-Client: api; never commit SUPABASE_HACKATHON_TOKEN; CI macos-26; skills JSON in caret/skills/<id>/.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"79ee0e2da00c6468","sum":"v1: .scratch/ never committed; Screenpipe sidecar behind a hard-failing last-N facade; Supabase control plane only; never commit SUPABASE_HACKATHON_TOKEN. CI keeps macos-26 (macos-15 type-checks #available). Caret.app runs own screenpipe@0.4.50 :3031; no CaretProjectRoot: no-op.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fb9536a9c704d4b7","sum":"Repo and v1 lore: SumMem at .summem/summem; .scratch/ never committed; v1 kept five upstreams, Screenpipe a supervised sidecar (launcher lease) behind a last-N facade that hard-fails when down or empty; Supabase is control plane only; never commit SUPABASE_HACKATHON_TOKEN.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5e2a432b193b2a33","sum":"Repo setup and v1 lore: SumMem at .summem/summem; .scratch/ never committed; v1 kept five upstreams with Screenpipe as a sidecar plus last-N facade.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"13a625ab21eb3fe9","sum":"SumMem 0.12.0 lives at .summem/summem (AGENTS.md Project Memory block is the write rule); .scratch/ is gitignored local scratch, never committed.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T170845Z-b7aad83361017857","text":"Onboarded SumMem 0.12.0 as .summem/summem (not a packages/ pin); AGENTS.md Project Memory block is the write rule.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T172705Z-bea3983b0d18183c","text":".scratch/ is gitignored local scratch (exports, dumps); do not commit it","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ab8c7585980a9874","sum":"v1 Caret keeps five upstreams (KeyType, GhostType, Computer Use Jev, Skyvern, Screenpipe); Screenpipe history is a sidecar plus last-N facade, never vendored, no TCC inherited from its CLI.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T173934Z-80f0ac884170d4c1","text":"Caret keeps five upstreams: KeyType, GhostType, Computer Use Jev, Skyvern and Screenpipe. docs/input-pipeline.md defines the proposed shared Jev/context/workflow handoff; the current action UI does not call the Python CLI.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T174647Z-c6a318f44bd68335","text":"Screenpipe history for Caret is sidecar plus facade (last N minutes/windows); do not vendor current engine or inherit TCC from their CLI","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"05674c45506c1bae","sum":"v1 Screenpipe and secrets: last-N inference hard-fails when the sidecar is down or empty; Caret supervises pinned Screenpipe via a launcher lease; Supabase is control plane only; never commit SUPABASE_HACKATHON_TOKEN.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"a7b8b39bcec29186","sum":"v1: inference needing Screenpipe last-N hard-fails when the sidecar is down or empty; CI has secret SUPABASE_HACKATHON_TOKEN, never commit its value.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T174733Z-8bbd21a4d3d18747","text":"Caret inference that needs Screenpipe history hard-fails if the sidecar is down or last-N is empty; do not continue on a miss","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T175112Z-813e2fb0e5f124b2","text":"GitHub Actions repo secret SUPABASE_HACKATHON_TOKEN is available for CI; do not commit the value.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0988f580d7d5ff22","sum":"v1: Caret launches and supervises pinned Screenpipe (TCC stays on its binary; client uses the launcher lease); Supabase only as control plane, never for last-N or threads.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T175326Z-cc8628073d6c6682","text":"Override: Caret launches and supervises pinned Screenpipe; do not spawn revoked; TCC still on their binary; client uses launcher lease","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T175517Z-d3f766ae6d1e35f4","text":"Supabase earns a seat only as company control plane (identity, entitlements, kill-switch, structured facts); skill bodies stay git/Cursor plugins; never upload last-N or threads.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"43ee91e8384e1ba6","sum":"Mac CI: keep macos-26/Xcode 26 in ci.yml (macos-15 type-checks #available); #if-gate new SDK APIs. Caret.app runs its own screenpipe@0.4.50 on :3031, never attaching; clipboard needs --disable-clipboard-capture false; lease in .local/. No CaretProjectRoot key: supervisor no-ops.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fec1309988e3870c","sum":"Mac CI runs macos-26 (Xcode 26, glassEffect): keep the Xcode 26 select in ci.yml, not macos-15 (Xcode 16.4, where #available still type-checks); #if compiler-gate new SDK APIs. Screenpipe 0.4.50 keeps no clipboard history unless --disable-clipboard-capture false.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"54b806582777cca4","sum":"2026-09-19 hackathon was happy-path only (ship, do not polish, preflight must not block on niceties). Mac CI: macos-15 defaults to Xcode 16.4 and #available still type-checks, so keep the Xcode 26 select in ci.yml and #if compiler-gate new SDK APIs.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T175827Z-8c1a94d022e0b4f9","text":"2026-09-19 hackathon: GSD and happy-path only; ship, do not polish; preflight must not block on niceties","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T180736Z-4ff972dc89772e30","text":"Mac CI (macos-15) defaults to Xcode 16.4; #available is runtime-only and still type-checks. Keep the Xcode 26 select in ci.yml and #if compiler-gate new SDK APIs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"3a7837f8430ada51","sum":"Mac CI on main runs macos-26 for glassEffect/Xcode 26; do not move it back to macos-15 (Xcode 16.4). Screenpipe 0.4.50 keeps no clipboard history unless --disable-clipboard-capture false; Caret's pinned launch does not pass it.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T180843Z-c0da2dfb3d09eb5e","text":"Mac CI on main is macos-26 for glassEffect/Xcode 26. Do not move that job back to macos-15 default Xcode 16.4.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T181107Z-8c8e5b028a0a7d1d","text":"Screenpipe 0.4.50 stores no clipboard history by default; enable with --disable-clipboard-capture false. Caret pin launch does not pass that flag.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"82995c451c95a78f","sum":"Caret.app runs its own screenpipe@0.4.50 on :3031 (never attaches; a second recorder can stop the first); clipboard needs --disable-clipboard-capture false; last-N via .local/screenpipe-lease.json. No INFOPLIST_KEY_CaretProjectRoot: ScreenpipeSupervisor.start no-ops.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"aa7dada86df3ecf0","sum":"Caret last-N reads minutes/windows/clipboard, newest first, via a lease in .local/screenpipe-lease.json. Caret.app launches screenpipe@0.4.50 on :3031 with clipboard on; clipboard is a Screenpipe UiEventType input, off unless --disable-clipboard-capture false.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T181331Z-7829432da9c4fa32","text":"On main 3db8f16 Caret last-N is minutes/windows via a lease; Caret.app does not spawn Screenpipe. Clipboard is a Screenpipe input UiEventType, off unless --disable-clipboard-capture false.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T182537Z-ff4a55f19dd31fc9","text":"Caret.app launches screenpipe@0.4.50 on 3031 with clipboard on and writes .local/screenpipe-lease.json. history-windows/minutes/clipboard are newest-first.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7effd9669f8097f6","sum":"Caret.app starts its own screenpipe@0.4.50 on :3031, never attaching to a manual or launchd one (a second recorder can stop the first). INFOPLIST_KEY_CaretProjectRoot is missing from generated Info.plist, so ScreenpipeSupervisor.start is a no-op until it is added.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T183142Z-62bc24835e4cc470","text":"Caret.app always starts its own screenpipe@0.4.50 on :3031 and does not attach to a manual or launchd instance; a second recorder can stop the first.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T183914Z-5f4c9ce43ef55285","text":"INFOPLIST_KEY_CaretProjectRoot does not land in GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE output, so shipped Caret.app has no project root and ScreenpipeSupervisor.start is a no-op until that key is actually in Info.plist.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4a30ad9bb039ceab","sum":"v1: skills JSON in caret/skills/<id>/; screenpipe@0.4.50 (:3031) has its own AX prompt, /search needs Bearer SCREENPIPE_LOCAL_API_KEY + X-Screenpipe-Client: api; last-N hard-fails; xcodeproj IDs unique (Info.plist B100…62); make install needs packages/keytype.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"cf173c783d21b3d2","sum":"Caret skills: JSON under caret/skills/<action-id>/. Pinned screenpipe@0.4.50 (launchd dev.caret.hackathon.screenpipe, :3031, cli-darwin Mach-O holds TCC) has its own AX prompt, unaffected by Caret's grant. Inference last-N hard-fails. xcodeproj object IDs must be unique.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d8373d741af56a81","sum":"Caret skills: name/description JSON under caret/skills/<action-id>/ (not Apify SKILL.md). Pinned screenpipe@0.4.50 has its own Developer ID and AX prompt; Caret's grant does not stop it. Debug menu shows truncated last-2 via history-debug; inference last-N hard-fails.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"25648c3d0b258189","sum":"Caret skills are name/description JSON under caret/skills/<action-id>/, not Apify's coding-agent SKILL.md; Apify is not a selected executor. Niko QA/Preflight (2026-09-19) used only cursor-grok-4.6-xhigh-fast or Gemini 3.8 Flash.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T185053Z-ae95c44f0be90de0","text":"Apify Agent Skills are coding-agent SKILL.md (MCP/CLI/Actors); Caret skills are name/description JSON under caret/skills/<action-id>/. Apify is not a selected Caret executor.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T185221Z-b9280ccda04db89b","text":"2026-09-19: Niko QA/Preflight in this repo today must use only cursor-grok-4.6-xhigh-fast or Gemini 3.8 Flash (Gemini not on the subagent allow-list).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"458043431cd4683f","sum":"Pinned screenpipe@0.4.50 has its own Developer ID (screenpipe) and its own AX prompt; granting Caret Accessibility does not stop it. Caret Debug menu shows truncated last-2 windows/minutes/clipboard via history-debug CLI; last-N hard-fail stays for inference.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T190218Z-3dcac55ddd67aa19","text":"Pinned screenpipe@0.4.50 is Developer ID identifier screenpipe, not Caret; it calls AXIsProcessTrustedWithOptions and retries while waiting. Granting Caret Accessibility does not stop its dialog.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T190435Z-bd82100fe9b9695e","text":"Caret Debug menu shows truncated last-2 windows/minutes/clipboard via history-debug CLI; last-N hard-fail stays for inference.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1dc8d7a171a0b9ab","sum":"Caret runs screenpipe@0.4.50 as launchd job dev.caret.hackathon.screenpipe on :3031 via the cli-darwin Mach-O (TCC is that binary); its screen/AX preflights stayed false despite Settings. Caret.xcodeproj object IDs must be unique; a FileRef in a Sources list breaks xcodebuild.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"73ecfa7fb5d9e38e","sum":"Caret runs screenpipe@0.4.50 as launchd job dev.caret.hackathon.screenpipe on :3031, exec'ing the cli-darwin Mach-O (TCC is that binary), not the npx shim; it logged screen=false accessibility=false and System Settings ON did not flip those preflights.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T190651Z-7c7ff0f30e9d0baa","text":"Caret-spawned screenpipe@0.4.50 on :3031 at 14:03 logged screen=false accessibility=false and retried VisionManager every 5s; System Settings ON did not flip those preflights.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T191856Z-e383776735c95605","text":"Caret starts screenpipe@0.4.50 as launchd job dev.caret.hackathon.screenpipe on :3031; exec the cli-darwin Mach-O, not npx/node shim. TCC is that binary.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"23edfb00e1d611eb","sum":"After PR #11 (main merged), README/productContext/techContext keep launchd Screenpipe wording and the Debug last-2 preview. Caret.xcodeproj object IDs must be unique; a FileRef in a Sources files list stops xcodebuild opening the project.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T192245Z-7c3e6304f151c521","text":"PR #11 merged main; README/productContext/techContext keep launchd Screenpipe wording plus Debug last-2 preview.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T192513Z-736b08c59f95f4f1","text":"Caret.xcodeproj object IDs must be unique; a FileRef in a Sources files list makes xcodebuild unable to open the project","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"357d6a64e95bbcfa","sum":"v1: xcodeproj Info.plist B100…62 (57 TabCompletions); Screenpipe /search needs Bearer SCREENPIPE_LOCAL_API_KEY + X-Screenpipe-Client: api; vercel key is a bare token file; make install needs packages/keytype; Translate reads selection or clipboard, not the caret line.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"eb97d3ea4b169abf","sum":"Caret.xcodeproj Info.plist is B100…62 (57 is TabCompletions); Screenpipe 0.4.50 /search needs Bearer SCREENPIPE_LOCAL_API_KEY plus X-Screenpipe-Client: api; router tests advance a fake clock past the 10 s backoff.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8b70e773b2fa893f","sum":"Caret.xcodeproj: Info.plist is B100…62, B100…57 is TabCompletions; never give Info.plist 57. Screenpipe 0.4.50 /search 403s without Bearer SCREENPIPE_LOCAL_API_KEY (/health is open); Caret _api sent SCREENPIPE_API_KEY only if set.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T192920Z-0329343e8c4345de","text":"Current Caret.xcodeproj: Info.plist is B100…62; B100…57 is TabCompletions. Do not assign Info.plist 57.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T193615Z-bae439ab3f2c08e5","text":"Screenpipe 0.4.50 /search 403s without Bearer SCREENPIPE_LOCAL_API_KEY; /health is open. Caret _api only sent SCREENPIPE_API_KEY if set.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0394a3f3d78f5601","sum":"Router tests advance a fake clock past the 10 s failure backoff; Caret last-N sends Bearer plus X-Screenpipe-Client: api with the token from SCREENPIPE_LOCAL_API_KEY, SCREENPIPE_API_KEY, or screenpipe's own.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T193745Z-b26ffd587de72a56","text":"Router backs off RouterConfig.failure_backoff_seconds (10s) after a failed evaluation; router tests advance a fake clock rather than expecting an immediate retry. Provider presets patch their own module's post_json in tests.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T193825Z-36390ce7b0d562a4","text":"Caret last-N sends Bearer plus X-Screenpipe-Client: api; token from SCREENPIPE_LOCAL_API_KEY, SCREENPIPE_API_KEY, or pinned screenpipe auth token.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8267e3a9d1defc9a","sum":"v1 keys and skills: vercel-api-gateway-key is a bare token file; make install needs packages/keytype; Debug last-N skips Caret Debug, inference last_n_windows does not; Translate reads a selection or the clipboard, never the caret line.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0077b084d2383d9f","sum":"Keys and builds: vercel-api-gateway-key is a bare token file (CoreLaunchSettings envFile holds AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY/GROQ_API_KEY as KEY=value); make install needs the packages/keytype checkout or xcodebuild resolve exits 74.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T214418Z-9e6967d283b5b427","text":"vercel-api-gateway-key is a bare token file (not KEY=value); CoreLaunchSettings envFile is the KV path for AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY / GROQ_API_KEY.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T214943Z-7cb27000d0b12580","text":"make install requires packages/keytype checkout (CompletionUI); empty submodule dir makes xcodebuild resolve fail with 74","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f8e28d7f83c0c10b","sum":"v1 gateway skills: Debug last-N skips the Caret Debug window, inference last_n_windows does not; Translate reads a live selection or the clipboard, never the caret line.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260919T215111Z-04557dfeed12d63f","text":"Debug last-N windows skip title Caret Debug (matches showDebugWindow); inference last_n_windows does not skip.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260919T215901Z-031ebbfd04136a32","text":"Translate uses a live non-empty selection or the clipboard; it never uses the caret line. Other gateway skills still do.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7bf5604878e7f35c","sum":"B1-B12: keep Chrome's titled AXWebArea out of keys; gate path writes no SQLite; never edit a running bash script; never mutate w.nodes; offer expiry only in lifetimes.ts; routine proof 3 silent hits Balanced, 2 Eager; Jev text goes through a SnippetLedger.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6a73d3d79df2e435","sum":"Chrome: top AXGroup/AXWebArea titled (keep out of keys), web AX despite AXManualAccessibility refusal. Fixtures: makeKey(), stdin focus moves AX focus. Gate: no SQLite writes, flush on tick. findAll; 250 ms grid; powerd UserIsActive; departure once; ro .backup.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"4d23ece8fc1b906f","sum":"Chrome titles its top AXGroup/AXWebArea (keep out of keys), rejects AXManualAccessibility yet exposes web AX; background fixtures need makeKey(); caret-screen acts only in --act-pids. Fill recency: window before the form's last focus. Use RollingText.findAll; 250 ms tick grid.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0f5b9811057334dd","sum":"Reader AX lore: Chrome titles its top AXGroup/AXWebArea (keep out of keys), rejects AXManualAccessibility yet exposes web AX, posts no DOM-text notices (E1/E8); background AppKit fixtures need makeKey() for focus; caret-screen acts only in --act-pids, rechecks fail closed.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b99fccd1ca3e2300","sum":"Chrome: top AXGroup is named after the window title and AXWebArea after the page title, so keep both out of element keys (E8); Chrome/Helium reject AXManualAccessibility (-25205) yet expose web AX, Electron accepts it; web pages post no AX notification for DOM text changes (E1).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T100848Z-2317db88abe7ef57","text":"Chrome names its top AXGroup after the window title and AXWebArea after the page title; keep both out of element keys or every key moves on a title change (E8).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T100848Z-7a26e801e62c7446","text":"Chrome and Helium reject AXManualAccessibility (-25205) but still expose web AX; Electron apps accept it. Web pages post no AX notification for DOM text, insert or remove changes (E1).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7284de3ea53779af","sum":"Fixtures and acting: a non-frontmost AppKit app posts AX focus only inside its key window (fixtures makeKey() before makeFirstResponder); caret-screen write/press act only in --act-pids, a subset of --only-pids, and rechecks fail closed on unreadable role/subrole/value/label.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T100848Z-bac1844f3b887c52","text":"A non-frontmost AppKit app posts AX focus notifications only inside its key window; fixtures call makeKey() (no activation) before makeFirstResponder.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T114801Z-32531afb7e4fe1e0","text":"caret-screen write/press verbs act only in --act-pids, which must be a subset of --only-pids; without it the reader only reads. Rechecks fail closed on unreadable role/subrole/value/label.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cfe456d6c1deaf07","sum":"Fill recency is the window before the form's last focus (the latest made Jev answer none); caret-fixture deactivates on becoming active, so poll lsappinfo front in GUI runs. RollingText.find credits the latest window: use findAll. Replay tests tick on a fixed 250 ms stream grid.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"55197345bf228f3c","sum":"Fill recency takes the window before the form's last focus (the latest focus made Jev answer none); caret-fixture spawned from the frontmost app held the foreground, so it now deactivates on becoming active; poll lsappinfo front in GUI runs.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T114801Z-431742a743596ba6","text":"Fill recency: take the just-left window from focus history (the window before the form's last focus), not the latest focus; latest-focus made Jev answer none on most fields once the user moved to another form.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T130715Z-7922f91e68f9ff52","text":"caret-fixture spawned from the frontmost app (T3 or a terminal) became the active app and held the foreground for a whole run; it now deactivates on becoming active. Poll lsappinfo front during GUI runs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"478a07b8a88c6346","sum":"Pattern code: RollingText.find credits a value seen in two windows to the most recent one; use findAll and pick the window that explains every round. Replay tests tick the helper on a fixed 250 ms grid of stream time like main.ts, or dense streams delay every transfer.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T143157Z-06f3c5b5c6254f49","text":"A value shown in two windows is credited by RollingText.find to the most recently seen one; pattern code must use findAll and pick the window that explains every round, or loop columns look like different sources.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T143157Z-9c4a82917dc22e00","text":"Replaying reader streams in tests: tick helper on a fixed 250 ms grid of stream time like main.ts; ticking only inside gaps >250 ms delays every transfer when messages are dense.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"648367d653fa1e3a","sum":"Gate path: no SQLite writes, flush on tick. Keep the pending watch's trailing debounce. No execFileSync in eval polls. Background fixture: stdin focus moves AX focus. Human input: powerd UserIsActive (B5). Count a departure once. Shadow store: ro .backup. Markers: structure.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c3649964eaa98e3b","sum":"No SQLite writes on the gate's event path (buffer, flush on tick). Pending watch: status text and a vanishing progress bar arrive in separate snapshots; keep the trailing debounce. Background-only fixture: stdin 'focus NAME' still moves AX focus. No execFileSync in eval polls.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e6572ec977c106ea","sum":"No SQLite writes on the pattern gate's event path (one insert stalled 11 ms at load 15-69); buffer and flush on tick. A --background-only caret-fixture reports no key window, yet stdin 'focus NAME' still moves AX focus; the reader sees leave and focus walks.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T143157Z-fc39a0364b9ecb3f","text":"Pattern gate runs on the event path: no SQLite writes there (one decision-log insert stalled 11 ms at load 15-69); decisions are buffered and flushed on tick.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T160236Z-60fc41a933501ea6","text":"A --background-only (prohibited) caret-fixture reports no key window, yet stdin 'focus NAME' (makeKey + makeFirstResponder) still moves AX focus; the reader sees leave and focus walks.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e21a3ad8c4a3fa82","sum":"Pending watch: a finished job's status text and vanishing progress bar arrive in separate snapshots; keep the trailing debounce or Jev judges a half-changed window. Eval scripts: no execFileSync in polling loops (lsappinfo every 100 ms added 150-250 ms to latencies, B4).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T160237Z-6009f034277d69a2","text":"Pending watch: a finished job's status text and its vanishing progress bar arrive in separate snapshots; without the trailing debounce the first Jev answer is about a half-changed window and is stale.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T160237Z-ba6e47628dfc0d66","text":"Eval scripts: never execFileSync in a polling loop. lsappinfo every 100 ms held the in-process helper's event loop and added 150-250 ms to every measured latency (B4).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"33f4ffb90faaf6ab","sum":"Hardware input shows only as powerd's UserIsActive in pmset -g log (B5). One window departure reaches the helper up to 3 times; count it once. Read the shadow store via sqlite3 mode=ro .backup only. Pending markers come from structure, not a sidebar 'Working' text (B6).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6aeaadf7a5a96e75","sum":"Hardware input shows only as powerd's UserIsActive in pmset -g log (B5). The helper sees one window departure up to 3 times (appSwitch, leave walk, focus elsewhere): count per departure; a return is a focused walk of a departed window.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T173801Z-d9e0d3a584c9d36e","text":"Human activity on this Mac: only powerd's UserIsActive 'kernel.useractive' in pmset -g log marks hardware input; agents' posted events raise WindowServer per-process assertions, and WindowServer per-device ones stay raised for days (B5).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T173802Z-3bfd0ad97555af7b","text":"Helper reports one window departure up to three times (appSwitch, leave walk, focus elsewhere); count per departure, and detect a return as a focused walk of a departed window, since focusedWindowId does not change across an unreadable app.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7e4af4b925d02c75","sum":"Read the shadow store only via sqlite3 'file:...?mode=ro' .backup to a temp copy (opening it as Store writes a salt). Agent sidebars (T3, Codex) keep a 'Working' status for a thread's life: pending markers come from structure, not status words (B6).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T173802Z-57d66219a60e6cdb","text":"Read the shadow store only through sqlite3 'file:...?mode=ro' .backup into a temp copy; opening a data dir as Store creates a salt file and chmods it.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T201044Z-85ef58a913b9161a","text":"T3 Code and Codex list other agent threads in a left sidebar, each a button holding a status text ('Working') that lasts the thread's life; pending markers must come from structure (enabled stop button by the composer), not status words (B6 census).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9041a0b28e5b0d45","sum":"B6-B12 traps: never edit a running bash script (mv a new one over it); never mutate w.nodes; offer expiry only in lifetimes.ts; fixture --foreground takes the front on 'activate legacy'; routine proof is 3 silent hits Balanced, 2 Eager; Jev text goes through a SnippetLedger.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"901960440bd057da","sum":"Helper traps B6-B9: leak-check is quadratic per line; mv a new bash script over a running one; never mutate w.nodes; pair focused:true with frontmostPid; fake-app pauses on a click; offer expiry only in lifetimes.ts; judge perf on real probes.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fd5a5290914f4366","sum":"Helper traps: leak-check.ts is quadratic per line (check one string per line); never edit a running bash script, mv a new one over it; never mutate w.nodes (WeakMap caches per state); focused:true from a request walk needs model.frontmostPid too.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d6128635107f5dca","sum":"Long-input traps: leak-check.ts hashes every word-bounded substring per line (quadratic; 50 KB NDJSON lines never finish, check one string per line); never edit a running bash script in place, write a new file and mv it over (B6).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T201045Z-36d6a210e08a778d","text":"leak-check.ts hashes every word-bounded substring of each line (quadratic in line length): an NDJSON with 50 KB lines never finishes; check one string per line instead.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T201045Z-88beaae782960744","text":"Never edit a running bash script in place (bash reads it as it runs); write a new file and mv it over, as B6 did with run-audit.sh mid-audit.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"894a99a3e4795948","sum":"Screen model: apply builds a new WindowState and nodes Map per snapshot (candidates.ts/descriptor.ts cache per state in WeakMaps), so never mutate w.nodes; a request walk says focused:true for a background app's window, so pair model.focusedWindowId with frontmostPid.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T201045Z-f95178d8fbcf4b52","text":"ScreenModel.apply builds a new WindowState and nodes Map per snapshot; candidates.ts and descriptor.ts cache per-state indexes in WeakMaps, so never mutate w.nodes in place.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T223858Z-64661b6aeffb7a85","text":"caret-screen's request walk (AppWorker walkWindow .request) reports focused:true for a background app's own focused window, so the helper's model.focusedWindowId alone does not mean the user is there; check model.frontmostPid (from appSwitch and frontmost focus events) too.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d3f84837adf559a9","sum":"Helper lore B8-B9: fake-app executor pauses on a click, not a key; offer expiry only in offers/lifetimes.ts; judge generator perf on real audit probes, not synthetic scenes; hand entry into a loopFinish settles first, partial matches re-offer the rest.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"364dcf1bfeba4910","sum":"Fake-app executor window is unfocused: tests pause it with a click in its frame, not a key; offer expiry lives only in offers/lifetimes.ts and records stay until offerWithdrawn (B8).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T231108Z-16725ff4ed3b6a48","text":"test/fake-app.ts's executor window is not focused, so a key userInput pauses nothing there; tests use a click inside its frame instead.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T231108Z-7306e773123a8d65","text":"Offer expiry lives only in helper/src/offers/lifetimes.ts: the host-offer registry keeps a record until its offerWithdrawn, and a loop going idle no longer withdraws its offers (B8).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4f388ef10e3dd3cf","sum":"Judge generator perf on real-window audit probes, not synthetic scenes (a 10x synthetic win slowed real cold calls, reverted, B8); hand entry into a loopFinish is judged after EDIT_SETTLE_MS: partial re-offers the rest under a new key, mismatch is stale (B9).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T021618Z-ea65f8fc10f79055","text":"Generator perf: judge changes by real-window audit probes (run-audit.sh PROBE_SECONDS, event-loop CPU via process.threadCpuUsage), not synthetic scenes; a row-sorted label index won 10x synthetically but slowed real cold calls (p95 5.3->7.4 ms) and was reverted (B8).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T032052Z-1661c0e7f0a95c07","text":"Hand entry into a loopFinish/routine is judged after EDIT_SETTLE_MS of stillness (typing passes through prefixes): partial matches re-offer the rest under a new key (offerWithdrawn reoffered + replacedBy); a mismatch is stale; all entered is taken at once (B9).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cacbd4934aaf6d62","sum":"B9-B12: fixture --foreground takes the front on 'activate legacy'; routine proof is 3 silent hits at Balanced, 2 at Eager; every Jev request goes through a SnippetLedger (privacy.test); chats give under half their text, so a field takes a kind whole or not at all.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ef7f0d6980690f67","sum":"B9/B10: fixture --foreground takes the front on 'activate legacy', 'quit PID' returns it; every Jev request takes screen text through a SnippetLedger (privacy.test checks); routine proof is 3 silent hits at Balanced, 2 at Eager, off at Quiet.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2c2a04358afd7dde","sum":"Fixture --foreground takes the front in ~100 ms on 'activate legacy' and 'quit PID' returns it in ~250 ms (B9). Every Jev request takes screen text through a SnippetLedger and sets req.snippets; privacy.test fails on undeclared lines or over-budget windows (B10).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T032315Z-0691c078778b7697","text":"CaretFixture.app --foreground becomes frontmost in ~100 ms on stdin 'activate legacy' (NSApp.activate(ignoringOtherApps:)); macOS 14 NSApp.activate() never did from the background; 'quit PID' hands the foreground back within ~250 ms (B9, run-activation-proof.sh).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T043507Z-396591a0dafeb49c","text":"Every Jev request builder must take its screen text through a SnippetLedger (helper/src/privacy.ts) and set req.snippets; test/privacy.test.ts fails on any undeclared window line, over 1,200 chars from one window, or half of a non-card window (B10).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f287a62811635a9e","sum":"Routine proof follows the level (Balanced 3 silent hits, Eager 2, off at Quiet; offers/settings.ts LEVELS); tests and evals built on two hits pass settings level eager (B10).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T043510Z-072d273b831b9d6f","text":"x","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T043537Z-5d59f5b5da2447c5","text":"Routine proof follows the level (Balanced 3 silent hits, Eager 2, off at Quiet; helper/src/offers/settings.ts LEVELS); tests and evals built on two hits pass settings level eager (B10).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"71f963f682e6c288","sum":"B11-B12 chats (conversation.ts) give under half their text, at most 600 chars per Jev request; the cap can cause wrong fills, not just blanks, so a field takes a kind whole or not at all, and close-on-miss stays outside kind groups (ledger charges every window showing a line).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"89eb27a1038b36eb","sum":"B11: conversations (conversation.ts) give under half their text and at most 600 chars per Jev request; the cap can cause wrong fills, not just blanks (cut meeting block, Meeting date got the order's Placed date in live-replay.ts).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T051909Z-10a9c6959d310436","text":"The conversation cap can cause wrong fills, not just blanks: with calibration sources relabelled as Messages it cut the meeting block and Jev filled Meeting date with the order's Placed date (scripts/live-replay.ts, B11).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T051909Z-f82b591e5e9c3894","text":"Conversations (helper/src/conversation.ts: chat/mail bundle, composer under 3+ message lines, or stamped sender rows) give under half their text and at most 600 chars per Jev request, however short; the ledger also charges lines a taken text contains (B11).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"5f02cf50c6404d08","sum":"B12 fill from chats: offer each kind a field takes whole or not at all (bare values padded the ~220-char budget and Jev picked a padding link at 0.76); privacy.test counts a line shown by any window and SnippetLedger charges per window, so keep close-on-miss outside kind groups.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T060232Z-ab20cd82e4a1331c","text":"Fill from a conversation offers each kind a field takes whole (every typed value, each with label/section/block) or not at all; letting values in bare to fit the ~220-char chat budget made Jev pick a padding thread's link at 0.76 (B12 live-run5, candidates.ts byRelevance).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T060243Z-76a84ab97345f4dc","text":"privacy.test counts a window line shown by any window's text in a request; SnippetLedger charges per window, so packing short spans after a miss pushed a 192-char chat to 104 covered on a 95 budget (B12). Keep close-on-miss outside kind groups.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
